  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National HIV-AIDS workplace legal framework and policies reflect new international labour standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From the national spectrum data, an estimated 78, 667 people are living with HIV (PLHIV) in Sierra Leone. Although the prevalence of HIV among the general population appears low in Sierra Leone, some populations are at higher risk of contracting and transmitting HIV.  The target population affected are socially marginalized and experience higher levels of stigma and therefore, they experience discrimination even at the workplace.
The ILO intervention will address the regulatory framework through the revision of the HIV at Workplace Policy to promote voluntary counselling and testing (VCT) as well as self-testing.</narrative>
  </description>
